# Firebase
# google-services.json is NOT secret — it is an app identifier and Google
# publishes it in every Android app. It is committed on purpose.
#
# A SERVICE ACCOUNT key is the opposite: a private key that can send push to
# every user of this app and reach the Firebase Admin APIs. It must never be in
# the mobile repo at all — it belongs on the server, or uploaded to EAS. These
# patterns are a backstop for a file dropped here by mistake, not permission to
# keep one.
*-adminsdk-*.json
serviceAccountKey*.json
firebase-adminsdk*.json
*service-account*.json
